Guidance:
Configure host networking for physical and service-specific network segmentation on new nodes. ¶ About this task Perform the following procedure if you are segmenting traffic on an unconfigured node (new host) that is not part of a cluster: ¶ Procedure ¶ 1. Log into the new AHV host as a root user using SSH and create a directory: $ ssh root@IP-address-host "mkdir -p /dev/shm/config/" Replace IP-address-host with the IP address of the newly created AHV host. ¶ 2. Create a cluster_config file: $ ssh root@IP-address-host "echo -e '{
 "arp_ip": "ARP-internal-IP-address",
 "dhcp_ip": ""
}' > /dev/shm/config/cluster_config.0" Replace: ¶ IP-address-host with the IP address of the newly created AHV host. ARP-internal-IP-address with an internal IP address from the subnet reserved for Kubernetes ¶ infrastructure network, for example 192.168.5.2. The newly created node must include a cluster_config file for the manage_ovs commands to work. ¶ 3. Log into the new AHV host as a nutanix user using SSH and create a bridge for the backplane traffic or service: nutanix@cvm$ manage_ovs --bridge_name bridge-name create_single_bridge Replace the bridge-name with a name of the bridge, for example br0. Perform this step only on a newly imaged or foundation setup. ¶ Note: After you run the manage_ovs -bridge_name command, the system shows the Failed to fetch gflags. Acropolis service might be down error message. You can ignore the error and proceed. ¶ 4. From the default bridge br0, log in to the host CVM and keep only eth0 and eth1 in br0: nutanix@cvm$ manage_ovs --bridge_name br0 --interfaces eth0,eth1 -- bond_name bond_name --bond_mode bond_mode update_uplinks Replace: ¶ bond-name with the name of the uplink port such as br0-up for which you want to set the bond mode. bond_mode with a valid bond mode such as active-backup. ¶ 5. Log in to the host CVM and add eth2 and eth3 to the uplink bond of br1: nutanix@cvm$ manage_ovs --bridge_name br1 --interfaces eth2,eth3 --bond_name bond- name --bond_mode active-backup update_uplinks Replace the bond-name with a name of the uplink port corresponding to the bridge name br1, for example br1- up . ¶ Note: If this step is not done correctly, it creates a network loop that causes a network outage. Ensure that no other uplink interfaces exist on this bridge before adding the new interfaces, and always add interfaces into a bond. ¶ What to do next Prism Element can configure a VLAN only on AHV hosts. If the hypervisor is ESXi, in addition to configuring the VLAN on the physical switch, you must configure the VLAN on the port group. If you are performing physical network segmentation, see Physically Isolate the Backplane Traffic on an Existing Cluster on page 195. If you are performing service-specific traffic isolation, see Service-Specific Traffic Isolation on page 209.
